Score an agent's importance, [0..1]. Higher is more important: it ticks more
often and wins perception budget when the frame is contended.

@param Agent            The agent being scored.
@param NearestViewerDist Distance to the closest local viewer, in cm.
                         A very large value when nobody is watching.
@param bIsEngaged       True when this agent currently has a Detected or
                        Tracked target — it is doing something a player is
                        likely to be in the middle of.
@param Awareness        Highest awareness level, 0 (Unaware) to 4.

Each of this AI's view cones as a flat fan: the focal cone (or the keyhole), the
peripheral wings and the rear-motion cone when the profile has them. Each rim point is
where sight really stops along its direction: at a wall, past glass as far as vision
gets through, at full range in the open. Re-traced when the eyes move or turn, at most
about twelve times a second, so it is cheap to call every frame.

@param bClipToWalls     Off: every fan is drawn to full range, through walls.
@param bOnFloor         On: the fans lie on the floor under the AI. Off: at eye height.
@param DegreesPerSpoke  Spacing of the rays (more rays near walls are added on their own).
@return False when this AI has no Vision sense.

Apply a piece of evidence about a target. Re-adding the same EvidenceTag
replaces the existing entry rather than stacking, so a repeatedly-applied
disguise refreshes instead of compounding.

Evidence is applied every perception tick, after senses and fairness rules,
and affects both the fused and smoothed belief — so a Clamp genuinely holds
the AI down even while a sense is actively reporting the target.

@param Target       Actor the evidence is about.
@param EvidenceTag  Name used to revoke or replace this entry later.
@param Operation    Raise (floor), Clamp (absolute ceiling),
                    Lower (settles Value below the sensed level), Invalidate.
@param Value        0-1. Ignored by Invalidate.
@param Lifetime     Seconds until it expires on its own. 0 = until removed.
@param Source       Free-form provenance label, shown in debug output.

Tell this AI that something happened at a place, with no known author.

Reports close together with the same tag merge into one belief rather than
piling up — two shots in the same room are one thing to investigate, not two.

@param Location   Where it happened.
@param Tag        What kind of thing — "Sound.Gunshot", "Evidence.Body".
@param Confidence How strongly it registered [0..1].
@param Accuracy   How precisely the position is known [0..1]. Lower values
                  grow the uncertainty radius, so a muffled thud produces a
                  wide area to search and a gunshot produces a tight one.

Emit a sound from an actor.
Only AI agents within SoundType->MaxRange of the source will be notified.

@param Source     Actor making the sound (player, NPC, animal etc.)
@param SoundType  Data Asset defining loudness, range, category etc.

Emit a sound from a world location with no source actor.
Use for explosions, traps, environmental triggered sounds.
Only AI agents within SoundType->MaxRange of SoundLocation will be notified.

@param SoundLocation  World position the sound originates from
@param SoundType      Data Asset defining sound properties

How far a sense reaches at a point, as a multiplier. Smoke shortens vision;
a noisy room shortens hearing.

@param SenseID "Vision", "Hearing" or "Smell". Anything else returns 1.

Set this sense's own wind direction, overriding the world's.
@param Direction World-space direction the wind is blowing TOWARD (the way the
                 air moves). ZeroVector falls back to the world's wind.

Report a contact event.
@param Instigator      Actor that made contact
@param Type            Contact type
@param Strength        Intensity 0-1
@param bPersistent     True = ongoing (overlap). Stays active until EndTouchContact() called.
@param ContactLocation World position of contact point (defaults to instigator location)

Report an explicit vibration event (explosion, impact, vehicle crash etc).
These are stronger than footstep polling — instant full-strength signal.
@param Location     World position of the vibration source
@param Strength     Signal strength 0-1 (explosion=1.0, heavy footstep=0.4)
@param Surface      Surface type that produced the vibration
